  "title": "YouTube preview size excessive ?",
  "content": "<p>When you type a YouTube URL while creating a post, you get a nice little preview:</p><figure><img alt=\"\" src=\"https://uploads-eu-west-1.insided.com/stmicroelectronics-en/attachment/5a40d89e-fb21-439f-9405-b7df5fb39d02.png\" /></figure><p>But when it’s actually posted, it becomes <strong>huge</strong>:</p><figure><img alt=\"\" src=\"https://uploads-eu-west-1.insided.com/stmicroelectronics-en/attachment/8216de73-0230-46d4-b2cf-3977d1fe8c3f.png\" /></figure><p> </p><p>I think this is excessive - especially when linking multiple videos!</p><p> </p><p>See also:</p><oembed url=\"https://community.st.com/feedback-forum-118/can-no-longer-resize-inserted-images-166205\"></oembed><p> </p>",
